WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.206 --> 00:00:03.706
(uptempo acoustic music)

00:00:13.652 --> 00:00:16.446
- Hi, I'm Hannah, your
friendly neighborhood wine mom,

00:00:16.446 --> 00:00:18.083
and if you're anything
like me, you believe that

00:00:18.083 --> 00:00:20.691
a glass of wine at eight
PM, every once in awhile,

00:00:20.691 --> 00:00:22.937
don't get crazy, makes you a better mom.

00:00:22.937 --> 00:00:25.058
So pour yourself a glass and let's talk.

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:27.268
By the way, did you
see we fixed the intro?

00:00:27.268 --> 00:00:28.868
Tonight, we're drinking rose.

00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:30.466
I bought my rose a little dress,

00:00:30.466 --> 00:00:32.867
because one of us should
be fancy, am I right?

00:00:32.867 --> 00:00:34.352
I just talked to my wine.

00:00:34.352 --> 00:00:36.829
So there's something I've
been dying to tell you guys,

00:00:36.829 --> 00:00:38.787
but first, you need a
little bit of backstory.

00:00:38.787 --> 00:00:40.272
Both my kids go to daycare,

00:00:40.272 --> 00:00:42.187
and they go to daycare near where I work,

00:00:42.187 --> 00:00:43.889
so I drop them off every morning.

00:00:43.889 --> 00:00:46.654
And every morning, I see
this cute little old lady.

00:00:46.654 --> 00:00:48.932
I smile and I wave hello.

00:00:48.932 --> 00:00:52.621
And every morning, she
gives me this death glare.

00:00:52.621 --> 00:00:53.704
Just, like...

00:00:55.372 --> 00:00:58.098
Whoa, this cute old
lady, what the heck, man.

00:00:58.098 --> 00:01:00.164
But I realize, she's not looking at me,

00:01:00.164 --> 00:01:02.067
she's looking at my hair.

00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:03.515
Because I have blue hair.

00:01:03.515 --> 00:01:05.398
This is a hot topic on all of the comments

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:08.494
on all these videos, too, so
I figure it's a perfect time

00:01:08.494 --> 00:01:09.806
to talk about this.

00:01:09.806 --> 00:01:12.337
Let's talk about the worst
things about judgy parents.

00:01:12.337 --> 00:01:14.845
So let's start off with
what that old woman

00:01:14.845 --> 00:01:17.881
was judging me for, colored hair.

00:01:17.881 --> 00:01:21.617
In every video ever that I'm
in, there's some commentor

00:01:21.617 --> 00:01:23.028
who says something like,

00:01:23.028 --> 00:01:24.603
(in a deep voice) Ooh, she's a mom,

00:01:24.603 --> 00:01:26.392
she shouldn't have blue hair.

00:01:26.392 --> 00:01:29.642
My favorite color is blue,
so when I dyed my hair blue,

00:01:29.642 --> 00:01:33.136
it just unlocked this
whole wave of confidence

00:01:33.136 --> 00:01:36.234
and happiness, and it
benefits my kids so much more

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:38.292
to have a happy, confident mom.

00:01:38.292 --> 00:01:41.136
So any moms out there with colored hair,

00:01:41.136 --> 00:01:42.798
this one's for you.

00:01:42.798 --> 00:01:45.886
I got a wine mustache from that one.

00:01:45.886 --> 00:01:47.623
Next, your age.

00:01:47.623 --> 00:01:49.781
I was pretty young when I had my first,

00:01:49.781 --> 00:01:51.295
and I looked very young.

00:01:51.295 --> 00:01:53.664
So I would get all these strangers,

00:01:53.664 --> 00:01:55.816
like, at the park with their kids,

00:01:55.816 --> 00:01:59.152
they would come up to me and
kneel down on my son's level,

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:01.020
and be like, where's your dad?

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:04.374
Where's your dad, I don't know, what?

00:02:04.374 --> 00:02:06.914
I got shit like, oh, was he planned?

00:02:06.914 --> 00:02:08.336
Oh, was he an accident?

00:02:08.336 --> 00:02:10.470
Is the dad still involved?

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:11.816
Who's, what?

00:02:11.816 --> 00:02:13.376
For people who are a little bit older,

00:02:13.376 --> 00:02:15.433
they get the same thing,
like oh, aren't you tired?

00:02:15.433 --> 00:02:17.414
Oh, don't you wish you
had done it earlier,

00:02:17.414 --> 00:02:18.698
'cause you wanted a second?

00:02:18.698 --> 00:02:20.599
Since when did this become your business,

00:02:20.599 --> 00:02:23.701
weird random stranger on the sidewalk?

00:02:23.701 --> 00:02:26.531
I feel like people thought
they could ask me all these

00:02:26.531 --> 00:02:28.908
intrusive questions
because I did look young,

00:02:28.908 --> 00:02:32.220
and to them, the age
that they had children

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:34.023
was the proper time.

00:02:34.023 --> 00:02:37.055
So now, when I see a young mom,
I will go over and be like,

00:02:37.055 --> 00:02:38.976
hey, you wanna come
over and have some wine?

00:02:38.976 --> 00:02:40.409
Are you even old enough to drink wine?

00:02:40.409 --> 00:02:41.657
Can I see your ID?

00:02:41.657 --> 00:02:43.877
Just come on over and
let's have a glass of wine.

00:02:43.877 --> 00:02:44.710
Next.

00:02:46.036 --> 00:02:46.925
Something.

00:02:46.925 --> 00:02:49.606
Next, meltdowns in public.

00:02:49.606 --> 00:02:52.628
I have two kids, they are
four and one and a half.

00:02:52.628 --> 00:02:55.281
They're, like, pretty
bad ages for meltdowns.

00:02:55.281 --> 00:02:57.871
And it usually always
happens at the grocery store.

00:02:57.871 --> 00:03:00.324
My kids always meltdown,
what do you expect?

00:03:00.324 --> 00:03:03.585
It's like, character shit in every aisle.

00:03:03.585 --> 00:03:06.063
So you go in one aisle,
and it's Spider-Man cereal,

00:03:06.063 --> 00:03:07.017
you can't have that.

00:03:07.017 --> 00:03:08.948
Go in the next aisle
and it's Captain America

00:03:08.948 --> 00:03:11.461
fruit roll-ups, not buying that for you.

00:03:11.461 --> 00:03:15.348
Next aisle, they're
selling Batman sugar bags.

00:03:15.348 --> 00:03:18.482
Just bags of sugar with
Batman on the front.

00:03:18.482 --> 00:03:21.428
And so when they do, it's like,
what do you expect me to do?

00:03:21.428 --> 00:03:23.916
Should I just leave my cart and leave?

00:03:23.916 --> 00:03:25.314
Like, we need groceries.

00:03:25.314 --> 00:03:28.006
So, why are these other
parents looking at me

00:03:28.006 --> 00:03:30.383
with a disapproving look
and, like, muttering, like,

00:03:30.383 --> 00:03:32.440
(in a deep voice) Oh, she
should control her kids.

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:35.346
Usually, these parents
are parents of children

00:03:35.346 --> 00:03:37.479
who are well past the age of mine.

00:03:37.479 --> 00:03:40.439
Do they don't really
understand or seem to remember

00:03:40.439 --> 00:03:41.825
what it was like?

00:03:41.825 --> 00:03:44.588
We're not at a movie theater,
you're not paying to, like,

00:03:44.588 --> 00:03:47.602
enjoy this experience
at the grocery store,

00:03:47.602 --> 00:03:49.212
we're all grocery shopping.

00:03:49.212 --> 00:03:50.889
Chill out a little bit.

00:03:50.889 --> 00:03:53.759
In this situation, parents
should help each-other out.

00:03:53.759 --> 00:03:56.084
If you see me at the grocery store

00:03:56.084 --> 00:03:59.473
with both of my kids
melting, just take one.

00:03:59.473 --> 00:04:00.808
Have it!

00:04:00.808 --> 00:04:02.756
It's yours!

00:04:02.756 --> 00:04:04.635
Next, milestones.

00:04:04.635 --> 00:04:06.589
There are certain parents,
it's usually, like,

00:04:06.589 --> 00:04:09.435
the tiger mom type, who judge your child

00:04:09.435 --> 00:04:11.357
based on their milestones.

00:04:11.357 --> 00:04:14.373
I got all this crap with
my oldest son because

00:04:14.373 --> 00:04:17.827
he was two and a half and
he wasn't potty trained.

00:04:17.827 --> 00:04:19.526
And there were all these
other moms who were like,

00:04:19.526 --> 00:04:22.521
(in a high voice) Oh,
he's still in pull-ups?

00:04:22.521 --> 00:04:24.798
There are some parents
who think that their child

00:04:24.798 --> 00:04:27.537
should be potty trained
by the age of six months

00:04:27.537 --> 00:04:28.970
or something crazy like that.

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:32.272
And it's because they do
this weird thing where they

00:04:32.272 --> 00:04:35.055
hold him over the toilet
when they feel like they're

00:04:35.055 --> 00:04:38.407
about to crap or, it's,
I don't even get it.

00:04:38.407 --> 00:04:41.974
He's four now, and he goes
to the bathroom just fine.

00:04:41.974 --> 00:04:44.945
It happens for each kid at their own time.

00:04:44.945 --> 00:04:48.653
My kids' bowel movements
have nothing to do with you,

00:04:48.653 --> 00:04:51.029
unless you would like to
come clean them up for me.

00:04:51.029 --> 00:04:52.172
You can judge all you want,

00:04:52.172 --> 00:04:54.240
as long as you wipe my kids' butt for me.

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.363
Next, childbirth.

00:04:56.363 --> 00:04:58.201
There is a certain subset of moms

00:04:58.201 --> 00:05:00.920
who are gonna judge you
for the way you gave birth.

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:02.620
They'll judge you if you had an epidural.

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:04.272
They'll judge you if you had a C-section.

00:05:04.272 --> 00:05:05.974
They'll judge you if you had a waterbirth.

00:05:05.974 --> 00:05:07.537
They'll judge you if you did it at home.

00:05:07.537 --> 00:05:09.428
They'll judge you if you
did it at a hospital.

00:05:09.428 --> 00:05:11.652
They'll judge every single
part about your birth

00:05:11.652 --> 00:05:14.925
that's not the same as the
way that they gave birth.

00:05:14.925 --> 00:05:16.818
Which doesn't make any sense to me,

00:05:16.818 --> 00:05:18.202
because the kid's already out.

00:05:18.202 --> 00:05:19.652
There's nothing we can do about it.

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:21.897
Like, I can't shove it
back in and do it the way

00:05:21.897 --> 00:05:23.588
that you thought I should have.

00:05:23.588 --> 00:05:26.573
So for both of my boys,
they were very short labors,

00:05:26.573 --> 00:05:29.288
it was extremely painful,
and I walked right into

00:05:29.288 --> 00:05:31.904
the hospital being like,
drugs, drugs, drugs?

00:05:31.904 --> 00:05:34.266
I got the epidural, I
did it in the hospital,

00:05:34.266 --> 00:05:35.722
that's where I was comfortable,

00:05:35.722 --> 00:05:37.364
and there's always that one mom

00:05:37.364 --> 00:05:39.686
who you tell them your birth
experience, and they're like,

00:05:39.686 --> 00:05:44.460
(in a high voice) Oh, well I
had mine at home, with no meds.

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:46.086
Like they're better than you.

00:05:46.086 --> 00:05:47.548
We both got it out!

00:05:47.548 --> 00:05:49.580
I don't care how yours came out,

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:50.759
I don't care where you were.

00:05:50.759 --> 00:05:52.346
Why do you care where mine was?

00:05:52.346 --> 00:05:53.948
If I see a baby, I'm not like,

00:05:53.948 --> 00:05:56.910
hmm, I wonder how it came
out of its mom's vagina.

00:05:56.910 --> 00:06:01.077
I don't give a flying
hoot about the birth plan.

00:06:01.077 --> 00:06:02.793
Did I just say flying hoot?

00:06:02.793 --> 00:06:05.799
But the worst part about judgy parents,

00:06:05.799 --> 00:06:07.501
is that we're all judgy parents.

00:06:07.501 --> 00:06:09.751
I'm judging judgy parents right now,

00:06:09.751 --> 00:06:12.215
y'all are gonna judge me in the comments,

00:06:12.215 --> 00:06:15.220
you are gonna judge
each-other in the comments.

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:17.355
So let's just all stop.

00:06:17.355 --> 00:06:21.520
We're all on this crap
rocket ride of parenthood,

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:23.567
let's be nice to each-other.

00:06:23.567 --> 00:06:25.534
If you see something that you wanna judge,

00:06:25.534 --> 00:06:27.351
save it for something interesting

00:06:27.351 --> 00:06:29.165
to tell your significant other.

00:06:29.165 --> 00:06:30.384
Hey, guess what I saw,

00:06:30.384 --> 00:06:32.823
some dummy talking about judgy parents.

00:06:32.823 --> 00:06:36.706
She was so dumb, she had
stupid hair, blah blah blah.

00:06:36.706 --> 00:06:39.940
It's perfectly acceptable to be judgy,

00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:42.104
but it's not okay to be mean.

00:06:42.104 --> 00:06:44.390
So that's all I got for today.

00:06:44.390 --> 00:06:46.610
I'm Hannah, your friendly
neighborhood wine mom.

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:48.529
It should be interesting
to see the comments

00:06:48.529 --> 00:06:50.739
on this video, let's try to keep it nice.

00:06:50.739 --> 00:06:53.115
'Cause I read them, I
appreciate them, and as always,

00:06:53.115 --> 00:06:54.868
if there's anything you
want me to talk about,

00:06:54.868 --> 00:06:56.366
leave it in the comments.

00:06:56.366 --> 00:06:58.152
And if you have something mean to say,

00:06:58.152 --> 00:07:00.821
take that to Twitter, because
I don't have a Twitter

00:07:00.821 --> 00:07:02.512
and I don't know how to use it.

00:07:02.512 --> 00:07:04.345
So, 'til next time!

